FORECAST TASK EXTRACTION
{"requirement": "Will adoption increase by 2027-01-31?", "as_of_date": "2026-10-27", "central_question": "", "declared_horizon": "", "baseline_defaulted": false}

Return only JSON {"horizon_date":"YYYY-MM-DD","source_field":"requirement|central_question|declared_horizon","source_quote":"exact supporting input substring"}. Interpret the overall forecast objective, not baseline/history dates or secondary binary milestones. The original requirement wins over conflicting derived hints. If no endpoint is specified or inferable, use null for horizon_date. Do not invent a default or rewrite the request. Dates must be complete ISO calendar dates.

FORECAST TASK REVIEW
{"inputs": {"requirement": "Will adoption increase by 2027-01-31?", "as_of_date": "2026-10-27", "central_question": "", "declared_horizon": "", "baseline_defaulted": false}, "candidate": {"horizon_date": "2027-01-31", "source_field": "requirement", "source_quote": "2027-01-31"}}

Return only JSON {"faithful":true|false,"complete":true|false,"issues":[]}. Independently check that this endpoint is the overall original forecast target, not the baseline, an example or an intermediate milestone. A source quote must actually support the proposed date. Reject conflicts with the original request, invented deadlines, or missing/ambiguous endpoints.
